<ArticleLayout
  title="When to record a string part instead of using a library"
  description="Decide by musical function: which details need a performer, which need repeatable control, and where a hybrid part is the more honest answer."
  canonicalPath="/sound-design/when-to-record-strings-instead-of-using-a-library/"
  section="Sound Design"
  sectionPath="/sound-design/"
  readingTime="8 min read"
  method="This is a decision framework grounded in how multisampling works and what live recording adds. It is not a comparison of named commercial libraries, and it makes no claim that one approach is universally more realistic."
